{
  "summary": "Logs automatic chainstate compaction start and completion by default, and checks available filesystem disk space before running background compaction. If available disk space is less than the chain's assumed chainstate size, compaction is skipped and a warning is logged.",
  "problem": "Full LevelDB compaction can temporarily require nearly double the database's disk space before old SST files are deleted. If a node has low disk space, automatic background compaction can completely fill the filesystem, leading to node crashes or hangs on shutdown.",
  "evidence": [
    "Fixes #36585, which reported: 'Background chainstate compaction (#35465) filled the disk; node then hung after shutdown (v32.0rc3)'",
    "Author note in commit 19b1126d5d: 'Automatic chainstate compaction can use substantial disk space and take minutes, but its start and finish are hidden unless -debug=coindb is enabled. Log both by default so operators can identify the cause of sudden changes in disk usage.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
   "depends_on": [],
   "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "The PR now actively skips compaction when free disk space is lower than the assumed chainstate size threshold, rather than only logging a warning while continuing compaction.",
  "card": "This PR logs automatic chainstate compaction progress at info level by default and skips compaction with a warning if available disk space is less than the chain's assumed chainstate size. Full chainstate LevelDB compaction can temporarily duplicate database files before deleting obsolete tables, which previously filled the disk and caused nodes to hang after shutdown (#36585 on v32.0rc3). Skipping prevents sudden disk exhaustion at the cost of leaving obsolete UTXO data until more space is available.",
